# TypeScript standards

## Strict typing

- **Never use `any`**. Use `unknown` and narrow, or define explicit types.
- Enable and respect `strict`, `noImplicitAny`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`.
- All exported functions must declare explicit return types.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Variables | camelCase, descriptive | `supplyChainId` |
| Function args / input types | `*Input` suffix | `CreateFarmInput` |
| Return types | `*Output` suffix | `CreateFarmOutput` |
| Interfaces | `I` prefix | `IFarm` |
| Classes | role suffix | `FarmService`, `FarmController` |
| Constants | SCREAMING_SNAKE in shared files | `DEFAULT_PAGE_LIMIT` |

## ESLint

`@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` is **error**. Fix before committing.

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
function getFarm(id: any): any { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
function getFarmById(farmIdInput: string): IFarmOutput { ... }
```
